  "text": "term Variable Something that can take on different values. For example, different subjects in an experiment weigh different amounts. Therefore \"weight\" is a variable in the experiment. Or, subjects may be given different doses of a drug. This would make \"dosage\" a variable. Variables can be dependent or independent , qualitative or quantitative , and continuous or discrete .",
